C"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":18,"column":1},"end":{"line":20,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"There are two phases of testing: testing that the source code\ncomplies with the Tax-Calculator coding style and testing that\nthe source code does not contain bugs.","position":{"start":{"line":18,"column":1},"end":{"line":18,"column":1}},"key":"fr3bbREhdp"}],"key":"oFUrFw4UQc"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":22,"column":1},"end":{"line":22,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"You can execute both phases of testing with a single command:","position":{"start":{"line":22,"column":1},"end":{"line":22,"column":1}},"key":"uVovjyPOaN"}],"key":"opBtj7ZeE5"},{"type":"code","lang":"","value":"make tests","position":{"start":{"line":23,"column":1},"end":{"line":25,"column":1}},"key":"PLC7QroxMl"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":27,"column":1},"end":{"line":27,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"No messages indicate the tests pass.","position":{"start":{"line":27,"column":1},"end":{"line":27,"column":1}},"key":"WLDpv4RvVE"}],"key":"Ron2YsNmGX"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"position":{"start":{"line":29,"column":1},"end":{"line":29,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Interpreting test results","position":{"start":{"line":29,"column":1},"end":{"line":29,"column":1}},"key":"KcpFi0U2F0"}],"identifier":"interpreting-test-results","label":"Interpreting test results","html_id":"interpreting-test-results","implicit":true,"key":"PR2UN7Wfnf"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":31,"column":1},"end":{"line":36,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"If you are adding an enhancement that expands the capabilities of the\nTax-Calculator, then all the tests you can run should pass before you\nsubmit a pull request containing the enhancement.  In addition, it\nessential to add a test to the pytest suite, which is located in the\n","position":{"start":{"line":31,"column":1},"end":{"line":31,"column":1}},"key":"PxPV1pWnCl"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"taxcalc/tests","position":{"start":{"line":31,"column":1},"end":{"line":31,"column":1}},"key":"NoOM9aVQgP"},{"type":"text","value":" directory, that somehow checks that your enhancement\nis working as you expect it to work.","position":{"start":{"line":31,"column":1},"end":{"line":31,"column":1}},"key":"A8O5O5Zopb"}],"key":"vSRuAknhFb"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":38,"column":1},"end":{"line":43,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"On the other hand, if you think you have found a bug in the existing\nTax-Calculator source code, the first thing to do is add a test to the\npytest suite that demonstrates how the source code produces an\nincorrect result (that is, the test fails because the result is\nincorrect).  Then change the source code to fix the bug and\ndemonstrate that the newly-added test, which used to fail, now passes.","position":{"start":{"line":38,"column":1},"end":{"line":38,"column":1}},"key":"iiZ1Fw7Lgd"}],"key":"s5TVantYR7"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"position":{"start":{"line":45,"column":1},"end":{"line":45,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Updating test results","position":{"start":{"line":45,"column":1},"end":{"line":45,"column":1}},"key":"n8gGHu70yw"}],"identifier":"updating-test-results","label":"Updating test results","html_id":"updating-test-results","implicit":true,"key":"BzdQiz6daW"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":47,"column":1},"end":{"line":53,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"After an enhancement or bug fix, you may be convinced that the new and\ndifferent second-phase test results are, in fact, correct.  How do you\neliminate the test failures?  Simply edit the appropriate\n","position":{"start":{"line":47,"column":1},"end":{"line":47,"column":1}},"key":"vWKh6UeOXE"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"taxcalc/tests/test_*.py","position":{"start":{"line":47,"column":1},"end":{"line":47,"column":1}},"key":"omC8eafkMO"},{"type":"text","value":" file so that the test passes when you rerun\npytest.  If there are failures for the tests that write results files,\nread the test error message for instructions about how to update the\ntest results.","position":{"start":{"line":47,"column":1},"end":{"line":47,"column":1}},"key":"Zt0qhXi757"}],"key":"JhC9GjflaM"}],"key":"mWiLD80gtX"}],"key":"ENQDzEfgaH"},"references":{"cite":{"order":[],"data":{}}},"footer":{"navigation":{"prev":{"title":"Policy parameter naming and placing conventions","url":"/contributing/param-naming","group":"Contributing"},"next":{"title":"Releasing Tax-Calculator Packages","url":"/contributing/releasing","group":"Contributing"}}},"domain":"http://localhost:3000"}